    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": false,
    "title": "torcontrol: send -torpassword hex-encoded to avoid escaping bugs",
    "user": {
      "login": "jpk68",
      "id": 256658809,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOD0xNeQ",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256658809?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpk68",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/jpk68",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpk68/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpk68/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpk68/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpk68/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpk68/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpk68/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpk68/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpk68/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpk68/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "The Tor password was sent as a `QuotedString` with only double quotes escaped; as Tor interprets backslash escapes inside it, any password containing a backslash was mangled (or left the string unterminated).\n\nThe Tor Control spec deliberately allows the token to be sent as unquoted hex \"to avoid escaping issues\", as the `SAFECOOKIE` response already is. This patch does the same for the password, and also adds a functional test covering backslashes and quotes.",
