      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "i think the motivation here is good since hex-encoding removes the need for escaping entirely. concept ACK\r\n\r\nalso, the TOR control spec [explicitly allows this](https://spec.torproject.org/control-spec/commands.html?highlight=hashedpa#authenticate:~:text=The%20authentication%20token%20can%20be%20specified%20as%20either%20a%20quoted%20ASCII%20string%2C%20or%20as%20an%20unquoted%20hexadecimal%20encoding%20of%20that%20same%20string%20%28to%20avoid%20escaping%20issues%29%2E):\r\n> The authentication token can be specified as either a quoted ASCII string, or as an unquoted hexadecimal encoding of that same string (to avoid escaping issues).\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nre: https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36637#issue-6008559379\r\n\r\n> as Tor interprets backslash escapes inside it, any password containing a backslash was mangled (or left the string unterminated).\r\n\r\n#36374 is already underway to fix this specific issue\r\n\r\nthe two PRs solve the _same bug in different ways_, so whichever approach reviewers prefer may make the other redundant. this one avoids escaping altogether, while #36374 handles it explicitly. i find this PR's approach more desirable",
